--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 5d3ee37fe71cbde498bb77b0858c3b19, type: 3}
  m_Name: ASH_FieldManual
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ASH.Inventory.ASHFieldManualData
  coverTitle: SURVIVAL GUIDE
  coverSubtitle: Field notes - property of W. Black
  coverNote: If you're reading this, the world went sideways. Read it all. Keep it
    dry. - Grandpa
  tabName: SURVIVAL GUIDE
  journalItem: {fileID: 11400000, guid: 8816d105f865b574fb6240824464a4b7, type: 2}
  lockedMessage: You have no guide to craft from yet. Grandpa kept a journal somewhere
    in the cabin.
  totalPages: 12
  pages:
  - number: 1
    title: Air first
    text: Ash cuts your lungs like glass. Wet cloth over mouth and nose. Stay inside
      when the sky goes brown.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b2d8f939253cfa84689d313c6907d3fe, type: 3}
  - number: 2
    title: Clean wounds
    text: Boil it, wrap it, keep it covered. A cheap bandage changed often beats
      a good one left on.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 006a4b1a55d66f843a1ff3105d3f03f7, type: 3}
  - number: 3
    title: Fire in the wet
    text: Split the wood, shave the kindling. Dry stuff under the porch. Never trust
      the top of a pile.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7f648f4212a4e624cbe5a97e61bfd82b, type: 3}
  - number: 4
    title: Keep moving
    text: Don't sit down in the open when it's falling heavy. Pick the next roof,
      go to it, rest there.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 28b6e2f3fba7eac4e981f39b0141b444, type: 3}
  - number: 5
    title: A bow from nothing
    text: Ash or willow, the length of you. Two good ropes for the string. Notch,
      bend slow, oil it.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 79c8eebdbceb2c84688c03176af1db2f, type: 3}
  - number: 6
    title: Water you can trust
    text: Snow melts dirty. Creek water too. If it isn't boiled it isn't water.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 223a4794d770bc14a9f3c241a5a9ad11, type: 3}
  - number: 7
    title: Breathing in the grey
    text: 'Those old masks take a can filter. Pack one yourself: tin shell, cloth,
      charcoal from kindling. Change it before it stinks.'
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 41fa612123f26034092847d5ab65662d, type: 3}
  - number: 8
    title: Reading the sky
    text: Brown haze from the north-west means ash by the afternoon. Thunder in ash
      means get under cover now.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: d807407da9b10b34b995b9c7f97c4a7f, type: 3}
  - number: 9
    title: Meat and smoke
    text: Cook it through. Dry the berries by the fire, they'll keep for weeks.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 7b702bd5ccb8cd34d982e573cb086bac, type: 3}
  - number: 10
    title: Shelter that seals
    text: Tape the window frames, wet sheet over the door. A lean-to helps, but the
      ash still gets in.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: aa3c6371464f1fe4d91c72d38e906aa5, type: 3}
  - number: 11
    title: Night walking
    text: Lanterns carry far. Keep to the trees, count your steps between markers.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: b295d556182226a4d809e9f9fc2710c0, type: 3}
  - number: 12
    title: If I don't make it
    text: Head down the valley road. Don't wait for me. Love you, kid.
    sketch: {fileID: 21300000, guid: 9f39f1f23ee6c6a41b979c10d04452b3, type: 3}
